```bash lucio command=execute show_source=false stdout=false stderr=false
# hidden block to ensure a certain queue is playing
volumito playlist play "volumito test qobuz multiple albums"
```

### Notifications (WebSocket API)

```markdown lucio command=include path="./ONLY_WEBSOCKET_API_CLIENT.md" style=literal
```

When using a WebSocket API client,
the `notification event` command group provides
facilities to emit an event (`emit`),
to emit an event and wait for a certain response (`request`),
or to list to all events (`listen`):

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito -C aw notification event --help
```

For example:

```bash lucio command=execute show_source=false stdout=false stderr=false
# hidden block to ensure a certain queue is playing,
# near the end of the first track, so that we capture some events
volumito playlist play "volumito test qobuz multiple albums"
volumito playback seek 03:10
```

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito -C aw notification event listen --timeout 10.0
```

